  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This honeycomb cable hat is worked bottom-up in the round with an all-over "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "honeycomb-cable"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "honeycomb cable"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " pattern, fitting adult heads of 54 (56, 58) cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bottom-up construction keeps the honeycomb cells interlocking from brim to crown. The pattern alternates C4F crosses on rounds 2 and 4 with C4B crosses on rounds 6 and 8, offset by 2 stitches each time. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " method handles the full circumference on one needle. About 120 g (215 m) of worsted yarn. The honeycomb compresses to roughly 80% of stocking stitch width -- always swatch in pattern."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Worsted-weight wool yarn",
              "qty": "120 g (approx. 215 m)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "4.5 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 7 / US 7)",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm circular needle, 80 cm (UK 8 / US 6) -- for brim",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Cable needle",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Row counter",
              "qty": "1",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch markers",
              "qty": "9 (1 BOR + 8 crown)",
              "substitutions": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle and scissors",
              "qty": "1 each",
              "substitutions": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "16 sts x 22 rounds = 10 x 10 cm in honeycomb cable on 4.5 mm needles, blocked. The honeycomb compresses by 20% relative to stocking stitch. At 17 sts per 10 cm the hat is 3 cm short across the crown for size S -- this is the pattern where gauge is most critical. Block and measure before proceeding."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k -- knit"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "C4F -- cable 4 front: sl 2 to cable needle front, k2, k2 from cable needle"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "C4B -- cable 4 back: sl 2 to cable needle back, k2, k2 from cable needle"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "k2tog -- knit two together, right-leaning decrease"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Before you cast on, circle your size -- every count reads S (M, L)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cast on"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-loop"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on the 4 mm needle, cast on 96 (100, 104) sts (multiple of 8 for the honeycomb repeat -- adjust to nearest multiple if needed). Tail formula: tail_cm = (needle mm x stitch count) / 10 + 15. For size L on 4 mm: (4 x 104) / 10 + 15 = 57 cm; round up to 62 cm. Join without twisting, place BOR marker."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brim"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 12 rounds of 2 x 2 rib. Switch to 4.5 mm needle. After the brim, you should have 96 (100, 104) stitches on the needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Honeycomb body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "8-round honeycomb repeat: Round 1: knit all. Round 2: *C4F, C4F; repeat from * to end (cables on groups 1-4 and 5-8 of each 8-st repeat). Rounds 3, 4: knit. Round 5: knit. Round 6: *k2, C4B, k2; repeat from * to end (cables offset by 2 sts). Rounds 7, 8: knit. Repeat the 8-round sequence until hat measures 22 cm from cast-on."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crown shaping"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Knit all on transition round. Place 8 markers."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Decrease round 1: *k to 2 sts before marker, k2tog; repeat from * 8 times. 88 (92, 96) sts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: knit all."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Continue alternating until 32 sts, then decrease every round until 12 sts remain."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After the final decrease round, you should have 12 stitches on the needle, ready to gather."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Top finish"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut yarn with 20 cm tail. Draw through all 12 sts, pull firmly, fasten on inside."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Common faults"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Honeycomb cells not interlocking: the C4B round must be offset by 2 sts from the C4F round. If both rounds cross on the same stitches, the result is vertical rope cables, not a honeycomb. Check round 6 starts with k2 before the first cable cross."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hat is 4 to 5 cm too small: honeycomb compresses significantly. The gauge swatch in pattern is essential; stocking stitch gauge is irrelevant for sizing this hat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fatigue from continuous cable crossing: honeycomb works every 4 stitches on the cable rounds. Take breaks to check the offset is maintained; the pattern is repetitive but the offset is easy to lose track of."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Wet-block over a bowl; the honeycomb opens and sets beautifully when wet-blocked."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash cool in wool wash, squeeze without wringing, reshape and dry flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Try the honeycomb panel on a sweater yoke for an all-over aran look using the same cables."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}